-- title:
--   Toric p-torsion pairs trivially with identity-reduction classes
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a level $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^2\nmid M$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and assume $p\neq 2$; assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC` of $j$ lies in the level-$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ $q$-expansion field over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport-style integral model `XHDRModelAtP` at $p$ for level $\Gamma_H(M)$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, let $\Lambda$ be level data at $A$, and let $O$ be a `JHNeronObjectAtP`, so $O.G\to\operatorname{Spec}(R_p)$ carries a relative group law and an identification of $J_H(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the geometric function field with its generic points. Assumed, and summarised here, are: representability of the fibrewise-algebraically-trivial rigidified relative Picard functor of the model by the designation built from $O.G$, its structure morphism and its unit section, both over $R_p$ and after base change to $\mathbb{Q}$ (with the corresponding compatibility of Poincaré bundles); separatedness of the generic model; an Abel–Jacobi section $ajQ$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ whose pullback of the Poincaré bundle along any point $x$ is the line bundle of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the cusp section, and which sends the cusp to the zero section; comparison morphisms $kQ$ between the two base changes, the induced morphism $\bar{aj}:\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C\to O.G$ and a base point $\bar\varepsilon$ with their compatibilities; additivity of $O.\mathrm{pts}$ for the relative group law obtained from the representability datum; the statement that for geometric points $x,s$ with $s$ the cusp there is a degree-zero divisor equal to $(x)-(s)$ whose class is carried by $O.\mathrm{pts}$ to $x$ followed by $\bar{aj}$; and representability of the analogous functor for the level-$\Gamma_N$ model by $\Lambda.X$. The conclusion: for every Weil datum $d$ of order $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ on the function field $xHFunctionFieldBar\,M\,H$ — divisors $D_1,D_2$, nonzero functions $f_1,f_2$ with $\mathrm{ord}_v f_i=p\,D_i(v)$ at every place, disjoint supports and rational places in the supports — and all degree-zero divisors $E_1,E_2$ with $E_1=d.D_1$ and $E_2=d.D_2$, if the class of $E_1$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,p$ (the subgroup generated by the toric points at $p$) and if the class of $E_2$ admits an $A$-point $s$ of $O.G$ over $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ whose pullback to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $O.\mathrm{pts}$ of that class and whose reduction is the identity section, then $d.\mathrm{pairing}=f_1(D_2)/f_2(D_1)=1$.
--
--   This is the case $\mathrm{TOR}\perp\mathrm{FIN}^0$ of Grothendieck's isotropy statement for the monodromy pairing at $\ell=p$: on the Néron model of $J_H(M)$ at a prime exactly dividing the level, a toric $p$-torsion class is orthogonal, for the divisorial Weil pairing, to every $p$-torsion class that extends with identity reduction. It feeds the companion result in which the second class is only assumed to lie in the finite part, via the degeneracy maps to level $M/p$.
